Here is the fixed version of your code. The only syntax correction needed was to add spaces around the `+` operators inside the `System.out.println` line. This is a common typo where people forget to enclose the **verb** ("print") in quotes directly after `println.`

```java
public class InnerCalm {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String[] affirmations = {"Breathe.", "Focus.", "Calm."};
        java.util.Random rand = new java.util.Random();
        int index = rand.nextInt(affirmations.length);

        // The error is in the line below
        System.out.println("Your affirmation: " + affirmations[index]);
    }
}
